  "details": "The following presume you're on PC, which has the capability to modify the thread scheduler and essential graphic and compute features of Unity using its built in resources that is universal across all applications that use it for PC based systems.\n\nThe end-user may modify these files depending on the capability of their systems.\n\n１. Open file explorer.\n\n２. Tinker with launch configuration in the boot.config file [VRChat_Data directory] to your liking.\n\n３. Launch VRChat.\n\n４. Wait for EAC bootstrapper to conclude, and for VRChat.exe to open.\n\nOutcome / Observation: EAC will detect a modified VRChat client on the basis of the once-customizable configuration files being modified. These config files are now redundant in the VRChat directories for the end-user. If VRChat launches anyways with no errors thrown, the boot.config file will revert to the pre-modified values.\n\nThe following (extra steps) are given that you have VRChat already open or re-opened.\n\n５. Modify the process priority of the application of VRChat using either:\n\n• Task Manager (Windows proprietary)\n\n• Process Lasso (3rd party paid)\n\n• Process Hacker (3rd party free)\n\n \n\nFrom [Normal] to (preferably) [Very-High]\n\n６. Check the process-priority post change-attempt.\n\nOutcome / Observation: The VRChat process priority is now fully locked down, and due to EAC is now not friendly to built-in or 3rd party thread scheduling programs.",
